es-rgds-slideshow-wake: the slideshow screensaver wakes when its clock changes, not ten times a second

Between slides, the slideshow screensaver told the main loop to wake every 100 ms (SystemScreenSaver::
getNextUpdateTimeout: DATE_TIME_UPDATE_INTERVAL with SHOW DATE TIME on, STATIC_SCREENSAVER_POLL_INTERVAL without it).
Each wake updates and draws a whole frame, so an unchanged slide was drawn ten times a second across the whole canvas
(3072x768 on the RG DS Plus): 14% of a core, and the GPU's work for every frame on top.

The clock's text changes once a second when its time format shows seconds (%H:%M:%S, the default), and once a minute
otherwise. The slideshow now wakes at the next of those moments, or for the next slide if that comes first. Without
SHOW DATE TIME it wakes only for the next slide: the 100 ms wake was there to poll for lightguns, which the RG DS
doesn't have (the black and dim screensavers already wake once a minute for the same reason, es-rgds-powersaver).
Fades between slides still draw every frame, as before.

The clock's update accumulator is reset after each update instead of having 100 ms taken off: with a wake about once
a second, the remainder grew by ~900 ms per wake.

